# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CRA Annex I #4 (minimise attack surface) / #2 (no known CVEs at shipment).
#
# This is the BSP defconfig for the nine SD_CARD and SPI_NAND board profiles.
# It is not a Joral product image — but it is in a Joral fork, and an image that
# can be built from it can be shipped from it, which is why the hardening was
# extended here on 2026-08-21 (compliance plan item 13).
#
# The removals below are the subset of luckfox_pico_w_defconfig's that carry no
# board function on ANY profile: general-purpose transfer and archive utilities
# selected by the vendor defconfig with nothing invoking them. iperf3 3.14
# carries the highest-scoring finding in the product image's own CVE run
# (CVE-2025-54349, CVSS 10.0) and rsync carries seven; busybox's applets cover
# the script-level uses of wget and the archivers.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT REMOVED, and why it is written here rather than left
# looking unexamined: freetype, gnutls, libmd and the python module set
# (pillow, periphery, spidev, smbus, serial, ...) ARE these boards' declared
# function — the Luckfox GPIO/SPI/I2C demos and rkipc's OSD text rendering. A
# "hardening" pass that silently broke the demos a board exists for would be a
# worse trade than the CVE exposure of a board nobody ships. If one of these
# profiles is ever put into a product, that decision has to be revisited, and
# scripts/compliance/check-board-hardening.sh names it as an exception with an
# owner rather than passing in silence.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BR2_PACKAGE_P7ZIP is not set
# BR2_PACKAGE_ZIP is not set
# BR2_PACKAGE_LIBRSYNC is not set
# BR2_PACKAGE_IPERF is not set
# BR2_PACKAGE_IPERF3 is not set
# BR2_PACKAGE_LRZSZ is not set
# BR2_PACKAGE_RSYNC is not set
# GNU wget: busybox's own wget applet (CONFIG_WGET=y) serves any script use.
# BR2_PACKAGE_WGET is not set
